color-theme: genetics

=== layout: one-panel

# Fruit Fly Test Cross

@body

- *F: fuzzy* - a dense covering of hairs.
- *P: prickly* - sharp bristles.
- *W: waxy* - a thick, water-resistant coating.
- Lowercase letters mark recessive alleles; + means wild type.

A triple heterozygote is crossed with a homozygous fpw tester.
Offspring phenotypes reveal the heterozygote's gametes.

DCO means double crossover. CoC means coefficient of coincidence.

=== layout: one-panel

# The Gene Order Is Given

@body

*F -- 25 cM -- W -- 15 cM -- P*

| Pair | Supplied Value |
| --- | --- |
| F-W | 25 cM |
| W-P | 15 cM |
| F-P | 34% outer-pair recombination |

- The homework supplies the order and pairwise values.
- The table lists alleles alphabetically: F, P, W.
- For interference, use the two *adjacent* intervals: F-W and W-P.

